                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 22 at 8:16AM MDT until October 22 at 10:15AM MDT by NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "description": "At 816 AM MDT, Emergency management reported Highway 59 between\nHurricane and Apple Valley due to flooding. Doppler radar indicated\nbetween 0.75 and 1.25 inches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall\namounts of 0.25 to 0.5 inches are possible in the warned area. Flash\nflooding is ongoing.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLa Verkin and Virgin.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nRemain alert for flooding even in locations not receiving rain. Dry\nwashes, streams, and rivers can become raging killer currents in a\nmatter of minutes, even from distant rainfall.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFSSLC"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS75 KSLC 221416"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
                        "FLASH FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 1015 AM MDT THIS MORNING FOR SOUTHEASTERN WASHINGTON COUNTY"
                    ],
                    "flashFloodDetection": [
                        "RADAR INDICATED"
                    ],
                    "flashFloodDamageThreat": [
                        "CONSIDERABLE"
                    ],
