                "description": "FFWLOX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Los Angeles/Oxnard has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nEast Central Santa Barbara County in southwestern California...\n\n* Until 915 AM PDT.\n\n* At 612 AM PDT, gauge reports indicated Showers and Thunderstorms\nproducing heavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 3.5\ninches of rain have fallen. The expected rainfall rate is up to an\ninch per hour. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly, rock slides and mud slides are also expected.\n\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by showers and thunderstorms. Rock\nslides and mud slides.\n\nSOURCE...Gauges reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nNorthern Goleta, Highway 154 over San Marcos Pass and Mission\nCanyon.",
